// str_find_from(hay, needle, from) -> the code-point index of the first occurrence at or after code point from (Python
// find(needle, from)); -1 when none, from past the end, or from negative. str_starts_with_at(hay, needle, pos) -> needle
// occurs at code point pos (Python startswith(needle, pos)); false when pos is negative or past the end. Both borrow the
// text (no copy), so a walk over a long text stays linear.
