//
// Postgres-backed durable store for the graphcore store layer. Objects,
// the append-only ledger, and the state anchor live in a real postgres
// database; postgres's WAL + group commit own durability (one fdatasync
// per commit batch), so the M1 store layer stops issuing its own fsync
// barriers. Everything is under the surface — the wire ABI and the
// store-op semantics are unchanged.
//
// Impl: axis-codegen-bridge-rs/src/runtime/pg_store.rs
//   * pg_bytes_put(addr, content) — content-addressed object upsert.
//   * pg_bytes_get(addr)          — object bytes; empty Bytes on absent.
//   * pg_obj_block_put(block, index) — one committed transaction per flushed
//     block; index lines "<addr>\t<off>\t<len>" slice the block per object.
//   * pg_log_append(line)         — append one ledger block row.
//   * pg_log_scan()               — whole ledger, append order, byte-equal
//     to the old .gcore/log content.
//   * pg_anchor_get() / pg_anchor_set(value) — the anchor as a committed
//     single-row upsert (key 'anchor').
//
// Effects are load-bearing (CSE): pg_log_append is NOT idempotent (a second
// identical call is a second ledger row). The reads and the content-addressed
// puts are idempotent.

