// FBANK_V1 (fbank.rs): a frozen bank — append-only, deduplicating, shared by every thread (the Int is its address),
// no lock and no shared refcount (a read copies the bytes out; an Arc-shared read writes its refcount and contends).
// fbank_put(b, ordinal, text) -> id | -1 (a lower ordinal holds equal content) | -2 (full: Unknown(memory)); equal
// content is held by the LOWEST ordinal whatever the thread timing, final once every put has finished (fbank_holds).
